{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Xcode asks to “Trust & Enable” a macro","anchor":"Xcode-asks-to-Trust--Enable-a-macro","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" are compiler plugins, so the first build in Xcode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompts once per machine to trust the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" target. Approve it in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build error’s fix-it or under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Settings → Packages"}]},{"type":"text","text":". On CI, pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-skipMacroValidation"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — there’s no one to click the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dialog."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The first build is slow","anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux depends on ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift-syntax","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the macro system compiles from source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching ","type":"text"},{"code":".build\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or DerivedData.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring","level":2,"text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Something called ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatched from an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context","level":2,"text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated init"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation","type":"heading","text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag = false"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag: Bool = false"},{"type":"text","text":". The same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applies to combined declarations: split "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var a, b: Int"},{"type":"text","text":" into separate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declarations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"